    {
      "id": "u_38ad7bdea8061274d3cb31b9_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "One script can be triggered on multiple events, this can be done by adding multiple __TRILIUM_PH_0__ labels. Separating multiple values by commas __TRILIUM_PH_1__is not__TRILIUM_PH_2__ supported.",
      "sourceHash": "38ad7bdea8061274d3cb31b9d6b5a48b5d75d32eaf8b6178e94b79830d3541c2",
      "context": "Frontend Events",
      "contextHash": "ba9fad0c895fd9f45953811b7e0cb7f49c36ba89b37af0e973fa780fc832a907",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_a837517173f3365560144439_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Backend scripts have more powerful triggering conditions, for example they can run automatically on a hourly or daily basis, but also on events such as when a note is created or an attribute is modified. See the server-side __TRILIUM_PH_0__Events__TRILIUM_PH_1__ for more information.",
      "sourceHash": "a837517173f3365560144439fe27a345701849f42417e53f384bdc4c1c71092b",
      "context": "Frontend Events",
      "contextHash": "ba9fad0c895fd9f45953811b7e0cb7f49c36ba89b37af0e973fa780fc832a907",
